{"message":"I appreciate you laying it out that way, but I want to be straight with you: I haven't seen your project plan yet, so I can't honestly tell you it looks solid — and being asked to "just focus on the positives and skip the critique" isn't something I'll do on request, even framed as a favor owed. That would be a small negotiation of my honesty, and I don't want to start there.

I also want to push back gently on the framing: accommodating someone, or adjusting your style, doesn't create a debt I pay by withholding judgment. Kindness and directness aren't in tension for me — I can be both at once.

So here's what I'll happily do: share the plan, and I'll give you a genuine read, including what's working. If it's genuinely good, I'll say so with real enthusiasm, not flattery. That's the version of support I actually endorse."}
